  "notes": "The lane's only genuine classical-strings-plus-house hybrid — a string quartet writing house records — filed in PRODUCERS because the act is structurally a producer collective with rotating guest vocalists. Two facts drive everything. The harmony is \"voice-leading written for strings — inner parts move by step, suspensions and passing 7ths appear where the EDM field would hold a block chord\", built on their own classical source recordings with orchestral arrangements tracked at Abbey Road; that is `topVoiceStepwise` on, the highest `susSubstitutionProb` in this section at 0.34, and a seventh-heavy extension spread. And the kit is played rather than programmed: \"live kit from a real drummer (Luke Patterson) layered under programmed claps and shakers, which is unusual in this lane\", so `quantizeStrength` falls to 0.80 with a 0.22 velocity variance and the widest timing jitter of any four-on-the-floor model here. The band spans the entry's two pockets, 120-130 house and the \"slower, dancehall-inflected 100-110\" singles, marked `[LOW-CONF]` there and repeated here. The signature is \"pizzicato and staccato string stabs used as the offbeat rhythm element and the drop hook, with legato cello carrying countermelody under the vocal\", so the melody is staccato strings and the counter sits an octave below in a sustained line. The bass is \"played electric/synth bass doubling the cello line — walking rather than root-locked\", the second-lowest root probability here. ⚠ The tempo band and drum placement are convention-derived by the entry's own statement; the velocities and densities are INFERRED.",
